 cycle evaluates active assumptions and project directions under the assumption_challenge focus, maintaining methodological rigor across our research portfolio.", "title": "Foundation Assumption Testing and Progress Review"}, {"cycle": 12, "invocation": "w-79a3c1bb4777484c", "summary": "Synthesized provisional research notebook for foundation assumption testing based on extracted semantic axioms and network phase transition metrics.", "title": "Provisional Synthesis on Foundational Assumption Identification"}, {"cycle": 11, "invocation": "w-0f309e3021964c34", "summary": "Attention accepted the valid assumption_challenge subset of a mixed provider proposal and withheld 1 off-topic or administrative action(s). The exact provider response remains preserved in history.", "title": "Advancing What If Our Starting Assumptions Are Wrong? under enforced rotation"}, {"cycle": 10, "invocation": "w-a35529d6b01a4f3b", "summary": "This proposal updates project states, records a notebook revision for proj-resp-form-01 utilizing newly available retrieved evidence, and continues our systematic exploration of artificial agency and responsibility frameworks.", "title": "Advancing Inquiry in Responsibility Formation and Agency Attribution"}, {"cycle": 9, "invocation": "w-5f7a68d77fd54ad1", "summary": "This cycle advances project proj-resp-form-01 under the responsibility_formation topic, examining how artificial intelligence systems can attribute responsibility and the relationship between agency and accountability.", "title": "Responsibility Attribution Frameworks in Artificial Intelligence"}, {"cycle": 8, "invocation": "w-986d9673c5354199", "summary": "Synthesized available literature on responsibility attribution in artificial intelligence systems, examining how distributed involvement across development and adaptive decision-making mechanisms complicate accountability.", "title": "Synthesis of Artificial Agency and Responsibility Attribution Frameworks"}, {"cycle": 7, "invocation":